          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %h3#suspension_by_representation_spheres Suspension by representation spheres
          %p
            Since a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            is, in particular, a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi BasedSpaces
                    %mi op
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi GradedAbelianGroups
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^\bullet \colon BasedSpaces^{op} \longrightarrow GradedAbelianGroups
          %p
            satisfying some axioms, then naively a
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Based
                  %mi G
                  %msup
                    %mi Spaces
                    %mi op
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi GradedAbelianGroups
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_G^\bullet\colon Based G Spaces^{op} \longrightarrow GradedAbelianGroups
                  \\,.
          %p
            This implies in particular the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suspension+isomorphism"} suspension isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n\in \mathbb{N}
            there is, for each
            = succeed "-space" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mi G
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mi G
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E_G^\bullet(X) \simeq  E_G^{\bullet + n}(S^n \wedge X)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where in the smash product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \wedge X
            the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is to be taken to act trivially on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acts nontrivially. Since we may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
            as being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+sphere"} representation sphere
            of the trivial action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
            is graded not just by the integers, but by any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+representation"} linear representation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
